---
/**
 * The hero (docs/projects/redesign/design-export/README.md §1, "Hero").
 *
 * The H1 is the name and nothing else — no job title in a headline (constraint
 * 1), no eyebrow above it (constraint 2). The only decorative motion on the
 * whole page lives here.
 */
---

<section class="rd-section hero modern-skin">
  <h1>
    Matt{' '}
    {/*
      THE HERO FILL. An underline that grows into a filled block on hover.

      The bottom padding is load-bearing and the matching negative margin is why
      it costs no layout: together they extend the PAINT box below the baseline
      so the descender of the "y" stays inside the filled block and the reversed
      text stays legible. Do not add the horizontal equivalent — it produced a
      visible sliver of colour past the block when the text was selected.

      Painted with a background-image sized to 0.07em and grown to 100%, rather
      than with a pseudo-element or a scaleY: background-size animates on the
      compositor and, unlike a transform, cannot be caught mid-flight looking
      like a half-drawn rule.
    */}
    <span class="fill">Pyle</span>
  </h1>

  <div class="hero-row">
    <p class="hero-statement">
      This site is an experiment in building the web for its newest readers, and publishing what
      they see.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-agent">
      <span class="hero-agent-copy">Reading this as an agent?<br />Start here.</span>
      <a href="/llms.txt" class="hero-agent-link">llms.txt</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: 78px; }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(74px, 12vw, 176px);
    line-height: .92;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
    color: var(--ink);
    animation: riseIn .7s ease .05s both;
  }

  .fill {
    white-space: nowrap;
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 0 .16em;
    margin: 0 0 -.16em;
    background-image: linear-gradient(var(--agents), var(--agents));
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: 0 100%;
    background-size: 100% .07em;
    transition:
      background-size 420ms cubic-bezier(.2, .8, .2, 1),
      color 380ms ease;
  }

  /* :active as well as :hover so the effect exists on touch, where there is no
     hover state to enter. */
  .fill:hover,
  .fill:active {
    background-size: 100% 100%;
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .hero-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 40px;
    margin-top: 44px;
    animation: riseIn .7s ease .12s both;
  }

  .hero-statement {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 30ch;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 30px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -.02em;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .hero-agent {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .hero-agent-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink-5);
  }

  .hero-agent-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-plex);
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--agents);
  }

  .hero-agent-link:hover { color: var(--agents-hover); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .hero { padding-top: 40px; }

    h1 {
      font-size: 68px;
      line-height: .94;
      letter-spacing: -.04em;
    }

    .hero-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: 28px;
      margin-top: 28px;
    }

    .hero-statement { font-size: 24px; }

    /* One inline row on mobile, per the 390px prototype. */
    .hero-agent {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: baseline;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 14px;
      padding-left: 16px;
    }

    .hero-agent-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      padding: 10px 0;
      font-size: 18px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }
</style>
